From 47140964b7f3249a852a82c86b58bd7e7c17b143 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cody Ho <codyho@stanford.edu>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 19:02:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: simplify M4 validation and firmware encoders

Share mapping-coverage checks between admission and worker snapshots. Use named UAPI render flags, remove unused timestamp arguments and utility/page-table APIs, and simplify render serializers without changing firmware bytes or ordered writes. Limit core-dump masks to their consumers configuration.

Validated by a warning-free kernel build, 15 byte-identical before/after Rust encoder outputs, and M4 hardware checks for 1250 UAPI assertions, async bursts and pending teardown, mixed render/compute, exact partial accumulation, compressed ZLS, layered clears with both empty-tile settings, and delayed dependencies and timestamps. Boot 022 / build 042, kernel #32.

(cherry picked from commit b89448f873d8f1c2a07917448b927cb4a93cd013)
